---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = "/for/beauty";
const title = "Shopify SMS apps for beauty: routines, shades and reviews";
const desc = "Evaluate beauty SMS candidates with shade-specific availability, routine preferences, refund exits, approved claims and distinct review requests.";
const faqs = [{"question": "Can purchase history determine a refill date?", "answer": "It can inform a proposed reminder, but it does not establish usage, suitability or need. Prefer shopper-selected timing and suppress conflicting subscription, refund and support states."}, {"question": "Can I use Yotpo for a new beauty SMS program?", "answer": "Yotpo Email & SMS reached full deprecation on December 31, 2025. Yotpo Reviews and Loyalty remain separate product considerations; do not treat a reviews integration as a messaging platform."}, {"question": "Which beauty app wins this comparison?", "answer": "This page does not report a comparative test. Evaluate Klaviyo, Postscript, Attentive and Omnisend against shade filtering, refund handling, approval operations and the destinations you actually serve."}];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a href="/for" class="link">← All store types</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5 max-w-5xl">{title}</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9">A shade restock, a routine reminder and a review request have different purposes. Choose tools that can keep those purposes separate rather than treating every purchase as permission for a generic replenishment text.</p>
    <p class="mt-5">A workflow guide, not a tested ranking. Product scope checked November 25, 2026; confirm account availability and current terms before purchase.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <TldrBox title="Candidates by evaluation task" picks={[{"label": "Shade audiences", "tool": "Klaviyo", "reason": "Evaluate purchase segments and separate email and SMS permission."}, {"label": "Campaign operations", "tool": "Postscript", "reason": "Compare Shopify campaigns and its current Email offering with your approval process."}, {"label": "Regional coordination", "tool": "Attentive", "reason": "Evaluate email and SMS availability for your subscriber destinations."}, {"label": "Combined workflows", "tool": "Omnisend", "reason": "Consider email and SMS with optional web push where the audience wants it."}]} />
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Build the routine from shopper preferences</h2>
      <p>A purchase date does not reveal how quickly someone uses a product or whether they bought a gift. Ask for optional reminder preferences without assuming a universal refill interval. Keep product, pack size, shade, subscription state and last fulfilled order distinct. Use email for detailed approved product information when appropriate; send a promotional text only when its purpose matches the subscriber’s permission.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Proposed shade-restock rehearsal</h2>
      <p>This is a proposed fixture, not an observed test or a performance claim. Create consenting test profiles for an exact shade, another shade, a refunded order, an active subscription and an opted-out shopper. Restock only one shade and inspect the resulting audience and destination link. A replacement shade should be a clearly labelled choice, never an automatic claim of a match. Verify variant-level filtering and queue re-evaluation in the connected store.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Refunds and subscription changes take priority</h2>
      <p>Pause promotional refill reminders when a refund, cancellation or unresolved product complaint arrives. A subscriber with a scheduled renewal should not receive an overlapping one-time refill offer by default. Check whether the subscription and help-desk integrations expose those states, how quickly they sync, and who handles failures. Separate service responses from promotional flows and retain channel-specific opt-out history.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Approve claims before activating automation</h2>
      <p>Give a named reviewer responsibility for message copy, linked product pages and every reusable content block. Keep version history so an amended claim can be withdrawn from queued messages. Do not infer a health condition from browsing or purchase history, promise medical outcomes, or turn a routine reminder into individualized medical advice. Use approved product directions and route suitability or adverse-reaction questions to the appropriate qualified support process.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Review requests have a different job</h2>
      <p>Ask for an honest product review after a relevant fulfillment interval; do not promise a result by a fixed day or ask only apparently satisfied buyers. Record whether a message requests a review, promotes a refill or answers a service question. Check the permission and platform rules for that purpose. Keep incentives transparent and independent of review sentiment. Yotpo Reviews and Loyalty are separate from the retired Yotpo Email & SMS products, which reached full deprecation on December 31, 2025.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Candidates worth a workflow demonstration</h2>
      <p>Klaviyo documents purchase-based segments and separate email and SMS subscriber lists. Postscript offers Shopify campaign tools and now Email as well as SMS. Attentive supports coordinated email and SMS programs in supported markets. Omnisend offers email, SMS and web push. Ask candidates to demonstrate shade interest, refund exits and claims approval with your integrations. None of those broad capabilities proves a native approval workflow or a reliable routine model.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Check alternatives against current capabilities</h2>
      <p>Sequenzy documents Shopify order, refund and cancellation events for email workflows, with optional SMS available as an add-on. It may fit routine education if the required events and permission controls are demonstrated; a separate SMS vendor is not automatically necessary. Drip’s August–September 2026 release notes introduce SMS, so do not rely on an older email-only label. Firepush’s November 2026 notice describes a web push app that no longer offers email or SMS campaigns.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Pilot the purpose, then price the program</h2>
      <p>For a proposed experiment, assign eligible consenting shoppers to a reminder or holdout group before sending, excluding refunds and conflicting renewals. Compare net revenue per eligible shopper over the same observation window, allowing for refunds. Subtract goods, fulfillment, incentives not already reflected in net revenue, support and messaging costs consistently. Review opt-outs and complaints alongside margin. A reported attributed order is not proof of lift. Obtain current quotes using the same recipient countries, peak volume and required integrations; no plan or outcome is guaranteed.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Primary sources for product scope</h2>
      <p><a class="link" href="https://postscript.io/">Postscript channels</a>; <a class="link" href="https://help.attentive.com/hc/en-us/articles/16948569849492-Send-messages-internationally-with-Attentive">Attentive destinations</a>; <a class="link" href="https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/360024538231">Klaviyo segments</a>; <a class="link" href="https://www.omnisend.com/">Omnisend channels</a>; <a class="link" href="https://www.sequenzy.com/features/shopify-integration">Sequenzy Shopify integration</a>; <a class="link" href="https://www.sequenzy.com/best-sms-marketing-tools-for-small-business">Sequenzy SMS scope</a>; <a class="link" href="https://www.drip.com/release-notes/august-september-2026">Drip SMS release</a>; <a class="link" href="https://www.yotpo.com/blog/email-sms-migration-partners/">Yotpo retirement notice</a>; <a class="link" href="https://getfirepush.com/blog/targeted-email-marketing/">Firepush current notice</a>.</p>
      <p><a class="link" href="/apps">Browse app profiles</a> or <a class="link" href="/guides/campaign-restraint">plan campaign restraint</a>. Recheck any linked guide against your current destination requirements.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} />
</BaseLayout>
